{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BieJsX9c2SbbdjD5snqGwz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence Murday Cotts\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp\",\"url\":\"https://jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp/records/41864\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5\"},{\"title\":\"Quasielastic neutron scattering and diffusion in liquid lithium and lithium–hydrogen melt\",\"url\":\"https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering\",\"url\":\"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0\"},{\"title\":\"repository.ias.ac.in\",\"url\":\"https://repository.ias.ac.in/56008/\"},{\"title\":\"informahealthcare.com\",\"url\":\"https://informahealthcare.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14786430802422006\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"}]\n\nI ran one search. It did not return the Murday and Cotts paper itself, so I can't give you its numerical values. What the results show:\n\n- **The original paper:** Reference lists identify it as Murday and Cotts (1968), \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945. Other papers cite it as the main experimental benchmark.\n- **Scarcity of data:** One 2012 paper notes that few experimental self-diffusion coefficients for liquid lithium were reported in the literature, because radiation-based measurement methods carry higher risk.\n- **Temperature and pressure trend:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study using an EAM potential found that the self-diffusion coefficient increases with temperature and decreases with pressure. It also reports that its calculated values agree well with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure.\n- **Other measurements:** Neutron quasielastic scattering on liquid lithium at 500 K and 830 K gave self-diffusion coefficients consistent with values in the literature. A separate study compared temperature dependence from coherent and incoherent neutron scattering.\n- **Theory:** A later quantum-mechanical theory of liquid-metal diffusion was reported to explain the whole set of experimental data on liquid lithium within experimental uncertainties.\n\nFor the actual temperature-dependence fit, you'll need the 1968 paper or a review that tabulates its values.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51b3d680-e8c0-42da-9f0e-baf62cb9c8e2","uuid":"684e1b03-ec34-4413-a1cf-a068441d6acc","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:30:34.910Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence Murday Cotts","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DvzCRGqtKSEK9BUwTtWdgx","content":[{"title":"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/"},{"title":"s00231 011 0874 9","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9"},{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"},{"title":"jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp","url":"https://jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp/records/41864"},{"title":"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium"